    },
    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Only five per cent of women in Karachi, the country's largest urban centre, can access higher education and of these women, only about two per cent enter the job market\" said Dr Zaira Wahab, Head Phil/PhD programme, Iqra University. She and other women professionals and educators spoke at an interactive session Women Inc. organised by Aga Khan University Working Group for Women to celebrate International Women's Day. Her research highlighted the lack of opportunities available to women graduating from colleges and universities.",
